,"subtheme":"AI-led IT services & ER&D transformation","tag":"AI-Services","theme":"Technology, Digital & Telecom","tier":"1"}],"thesis":"A soft-but-in-line quarter — **IT-services revenue $2.61bn (+0.9% YoY, −1.2% QoQ CC)**, **margin down 120 bps YoY to 16%** on wage hikes + AI/deal investments + acquisition drag, and a **weak Q2 guide of −1.5% to +0.5% CC**. Americas (esp. Americas-2 −7.3% YoY), Health (−3.0%) and EMR (−8.9%) are the drags; APMEA (+13.5%) and Tech-&-Comm (+10.8%) the bright spots. The whole narrative is the **AI pivot**: a new AI-native business unit moving \"strategy → execution,\" the WINGS delivery platform, \"Reimagine AI\" services (advisory, data priming, agent orchestration, ModelOps, Sovereign AI, AI-DC), and ecosystem CoEs (an **Applied AI CoE for Claude models with Anthropic**; Capco won an OpenAI Partner-Summit award). Management frames AI as market-*expanding*, funds the investment through disciplined margin levers, and targets a return to the **17–17.5%** band (no timeframe) while returning **>$3bn to shareholders** over the trailing year.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":179572,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":1,"prev_zone_vpe":-0.6,"r":null,"s":"WIPRO","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"179.3","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"34.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-0.2","vpe_zone_cumul_df":""},"t":"basing"}},"s":"WIPRO"}